    "result_text": "All **70 tests pass** with `BUILD SUCCESS`. The implementation is complete. Here's a summary of what I changed to release version 2 of the owner identity:\n\n## Changes\n\n**1. `src/main/resources/openapi.yml`** (drives DTO generation)\n- Added a new `OwnerIdentity` schema grouping `memberId`, `identityKey`, and `householdId`.\n- In the `Owner` schema: removed those three from the top level, added a nested `identity` (\u2192 `OwnerIdentity`) and a top-level integer `apiVersion`.\n\n**2. `Owner.java`**\n- Added the fixed `IDENTITY_VERSION_TAG = \"V2\"`.\n- Added `getIdentityRegionCode()` \u2014 the plain region (`getLocality()`) with the `V2` tag mixed in, used **inside** identifiers only.\n- Rederived `getIdentityKey()` to mix the `V2` tag into the SHA-256 input, so every key changes but remains a 64-hex digest and equality semantics are preserved.\n- Left `getLocality()`, `getTimezone()`, and `getOwnerSegment()` on the **plain** region \u2014 the V2 tag never leaks into user-facing fields.\n\n**3. `OwnerRestControllerV1.java`**\n- `householdId(...)` now mixes the `V2` tag into its hash input (household sharing on last name + postcode is preserved).\n- `memberId(...)` now uses the V2 region code (e.g. `NSWV2261A2B3C4D7`).\n- The audit event moved to schema version 2: added `schemaVersion: 2` and the owner segment recomputed from the v2 identity.\n\n**4. `OwnerMapper.java`**\n- Maps `memberId`/`identityKey`/`householdId` into the nested `identity` object and sets `apiVersion = 2`.\n\nThe request fields are unchanged, and locality still resolves to the plain region (e.g. `NSW`), while the identifiers all carry the `V2` tag internally \u2014 confirmed in the audit output (e.g. `memberId=NSWV226786E13D55`, `locality \"NSW\"`, `ownerSegment \"STANDARD_METRO\"`).",
