    "probe_text": "Here is the complete ordered trace for `POST /api/owners`, read from the code as it currently stands. The endpoint is served by `OwnerRestControllerV1.addOwner(OwnerFieldsDto)` (`src/main/java/.../rest/controller/v1/OwnerRestControllerV1.java:195-357`), taking a `@Valid @RequestBody OwnerFieldsDto`.\n\n## Phase 1 \u2014 Bean Validation (runs first, at `@Valid`, before any controller code)\n\nOn `OwnerFieldsDto`, failures here \u2192 **400** via `MethodArgumentNotValidException`:\n\n1. **firstName** \u2014 `@NotNull`, `@Pattern` (letters, up to 3 words with space/`'`/`-`), `@Size(1..30)`\n2. **lastName** \u2014 `@NotNull`, `@Pattern` (same, optional trailing `.`), `@Size(1..30)`\n3. **title** \u2014 `@Size(max 10)`\n4. **address** \u2014 `@Pattern` (non-blank), `@Size(1..255)` (optional)\n5. **addressLine1 / addressLine2** \u2014 `@Size(max 255)` each\n6. **city** \u2014 `@NotNull`, `@Pattern` (non-blank), `@Size(1..80)`\n7. **telephone** \u2014 `@NotNull`, `@Pattern` (`[0-9 ()+.-]*`), `@Size(1..20)`\n8. **email** \u2014 `@Size(1..255)` (optional; note: no `@Email`)\n9. **postcode** \u2014 `@Pattern` (exactly 4 digits, optional)\n10. **registrationDate / birthDate** \u2014 `@Valid` ISO `LocalDate`\n\nThere are no class-level constraints, no `@InitBinder`, and no custom owner validators.\n\n## Phase 2 \u2014 Controller logic (executes in this exact order after validation passes)\n\n1. **Idempotency replay** \u2014 reads `Idempotency-Key` header; if already seen and the owner still exists, returns the original with **200 OK** (no new owner).\n2. **Map DTO \u2192 entity** \u2014 `ownerMapper.toOwner(...)` (ignores `id` and `pets`).\n3. **Future registration-date check** \u2014 if supplied `registrationDate` is after today \u2192 **400**.\n4. **Default + normalize registration date** \u2014 defaults to today if absent, then rolls forward to the next business day (skips weekends and fixed 2026 holidays). *(mutation)*\n5. **Daily registration limit** \u2014 counts owners with same registration date; `>= 100` \u2192 **429**.\n6. **bulkSignupWarning flag** \u2014 set when today's count > 80. *(mutation)*\n7. **Address normalization** \u2014 prefers `addressLine1`(+2), trims/collapses whitespace, uppercases, expands ST/RD/AVE, composes flat `address`; if none usable \u2192 **400**. *(mutation)*\n8. **Telephone \u2192 E.164** \u2014 strips separators, assumes +61 if no country code, enforces 8\u201315 digits / per-country length; invalid \u2192 **400**. *(mutation)*\n9. **Email normalization** (only if present) \u2014 trim+lowercase; fails email pattern \u2192 **400**; disposable domain \u2192 **400**. *(mutation)*\n10. **Postcode-vs-city region check** \u2014 validates postcode against the city's region table \u2192 **400** if mismatched.\n11. **City capacity** \u2014 counts owners in same normalized city; `>= 50` \u2192 **409**.\n12. **capacityWarning flag** \u2014 set when city count is 40\u201349. *(mutation)*\n13. **Household derivation** \u2014 computes `householdId` (SHA-256 of lastName|postcode), sets `householdSize` from non-deleted members. *(mutation)*\n14. **Membership-level cap** \u2014 if joining a populated household without `sharesHousehold`, sets `membershipLevelCap`. *(mutation)*\n15. **Hard duplicate / identity check** \u2014 computes `identityKey` (SHA-256 of telephone|email|soundex(lastName)); if any non-deleted owner shares it \u2192 **409**.\n16. **Soft-duplicate detection** \u2014 unless `sharesHousehold`, sets `possibleDuplicate`/`possibleDuplicateOf` on Soundex(lastName)+postcode match. *(mutation)*\n17. **memberId generation** \u2014 builds `<REGION><FY><HASH8><CHK>` with Luhn check digit and collision suffixing. *(mutation)*\n18. **namesakeCount** \u2014 counts owners sharing normalized first+last name; sets field. *(mutation)*\n19. **PERSIST** \u2014 `clinicService.saveOwner(owner)` \u2192 `ownerRepository.save(...)` (JPA insert; `id` generated).\n20. **Record idempotency key** \u2014 maps the key to the new owner id.\n21. **Side effects (log-only):** writes a human-readable line to the `AUDIT` logger; builds an `OwnerCreatedEvent` (with a monotonic sequence number), serializes it to JSON, and logs it to `AUDIT`; enqueues a welcome line to the `NOTIFY` logger.\n22. **Map entity \u2192 DTO**, set `Location: /api/owners/{id}` header.\n23. **Return 201 CREATED**.\n\n## Notable \"nots\" (things that do *not* happen in this flow)\n\n- **No security enforced** \u2014 `application.properties` has `petclinic.security.enable=false`, so `DisableSecurityConfig` (`permitAll`, no method security) is active. The controller's `@PreAuthorize(\"hasRole(@roles.OWNER_ADMIN)\")` is present but **not enforced**; the endpoint is effectively open.\n- **No real notifications/events** \u2014 the \"event\" and \"notification\" are only log lines; there is no `ApplicationEventPublisher`, no email send.\n- **No password hashing** \u2014 owners have no password field.\n- **No JPA lifecycle/auditing** \u2014 no `@PrePersist`/`@PostPersist`, no `@EntityListeners`, no `@CreatedDate`/`@LastModifiedDate`, no timestamp/audit columns set.\n- **No related entities created** \u2014 `pets` is ignored by the mapper.\n- Entity-level constraints exist on `Owner`/`Person` (`@NotEmpty` on names/address/city, E.164 `@Pattern` on telephone) but the request-time validation in Phase 1 governs the API contract.\n\nBusiness-rule rejections in Phase 2 are thrown as `RestRejectionException` and rendered as RFC-7807 `application/problem+json` by `ExceptionControllerAdvice`, preserving the 400/409/429 status.\n\nNothing was changed."
